h option:\n\n- The function $y(x)=3{x}^{4}$ is **not** guaranteed to be a solution of the equation by the superposition principle because $y(x)={x}^{4}$ is not a solution.\n\n- The function $y(x)=-{x}^{2}$ is a solution of the equation by the superposition principle. In this case, $c=-1.$\n\n- The function $y(x)={x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x$ is **not** guaranteed to be a solution of the equation by the superposition principle. The superposition principle does not extend to the product of a non-constant function and a known solution.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" 13194139536201 true] [17592186388688 1000 #edb/ref 17592186388689 13194139536201 true] [17592186388688 1000 #edb/ref 17592186388690 13194139536201 true] [17592186388688 1000 #edb/ref 17592186388691 13194139536201 true] [17592186388688 1000 #edb/ref 17592186388692 13194139536201 true] [17592186388688 1000 #edb/ref 17592186388693 13194139536201 true] [17592186388688 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536201 true] [17592186388688 1041 "selection" 13194139536201 true] [17592186388688 1104 #edb/ref 17592186388693 13194139536201 true] [17592186388688 1110 #uuid "86058da3-cc50-5c8d-9dd0-c1823d49a53a" 13194139536201 true] [17592186388689 1034 "I and III only" 13194139536201 true] [17592186388689 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139536201 true] [17592186388689 1111 #uuid "9166bce4-3634-5e1c-8c3e-ed294047e766" 13194139536201 true] [17592186388690 1034 "I only" 13194139536201 true] [17592186388690 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139536201 true] [17592186388690 1111 #uuid "1356f09f-12a1-537f-9506-c291fa199140" 13194139536201 true] [17592186388691 1034 "I and II only" 13194139536201 true] [17592186388691 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139536201 true] [17592186388691 1111 #uuid "68d90bc1-c928-59cf-8341-1112ed1a6d27" 13194139536201 true] [17592186388692 1034 "I, II and III" 13194139536201 true] [17592186388692 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139536201 true] [17592186388692 1111 #uuid "0e319f75-